#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:47
#: c1b65413fcb1456894e77b1f08db5380
msgid "What's new compared to Navio+"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:49
#: f9a2e91049de466a92ab3dcfc37c27f4
msgid "**Dual IMU.** Navio2 has two IMU chips to improve flight experience and for redundancy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:51
#: 69da5a26aa6047a8b898ee14140f3d66
msgid "**Improved MS5611 performance.** Transactions from other chips on the bus, which MS5611 is connected to, can produce noise during the conversion. That's why MS5611 was left the only sensor on the I2C bus to overcome this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:53
#: 4287ac53a3564e1185a8ae96c4f19f78
msgid "**PCA9685 PWM generator replaced with a microcontroller.** On previous Navio version PWM generation was handled by PCA9685 chip. Main limitation of this chip is the inability to control frequencies for separate channels. This leads to problems with motors and servos that work on different frequencies. To eliminate that problem a microcontroller is used. It allows to set frequencies for output channels by groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:55
#: da2ffa89e341473ba077a9011ab3a081
msgid "**PPM/SBUS decoding done by microcontroller instead of DMA.**  Navio+ used DMA to sample PPM signal which was quite heavy on system resources. On Navio2 a microcontroller handles PPM/SBUS sampling leaving processor cores of Raspberry Pi 2 for your tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:57
#: b04f0f185e8d46e8b92f0783783aeac8
msgid "**AUX SPI.** Navio2 is the first HAT to utilize AUX SPI controller on Raspberry Pi. Using two SPI controllers allows to distribute sensors more efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:59
#: b464bd9b86044725acec2a3951660e20
msgid "**ADC port.** Using additional ADC channels on Navio+ was not user friendly due to ADC channels being only available on pads at the bottom of the board. On Navio2 these channels are easily accessible on a DF13 port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-navio2-overview.rst:61
#: c999229efe7f465abcb93df7604b71b5
msgid "**Better Linux integration.** PWM, ADC, SBUS and PPM are integrated in Linux sysfs allowing for easy access from any programming language. Even deeper integration is coming in the future."
msgstr ""

